# scripts/gates_register_check.cx — the derived gate register, checked against
# the suites it describes (D49a, #1633; RULED: RS-27). Written in CX
# (AGENTS.md rule 6); one of the checks `make gates-manifest-gate` runs.
#
# A suite's gate status lives ON its [test-suite] element; conformance/gates.cxd
# is the cx-wide register DERIVED from those elements. This program reads the
# register's [gate-policy …] and the [test-suite] element of every corpus file
# the register can name —
#
#   conformance/{stdlib,platform,x,xap}/M.cxd   keyed [suite name=stdlib] M
#   packages/M/M.test.cxd                       keyed [suite name=packages] M
#
# — and prints `[$reg:report [$reg:check …]]` from scripts/gates_register.cx:
# the census line, then `ok` or one line per refusal (a row that disagrees with
# its element, an advisory element the register does not list, an element
# gate= the grader refuses). conformance/gates_register.cxd pins every one of
# those verdicts over described trees; this is the same function over the real
# one.
#
# Run from the checkout root (the globs and the [?lib] below are cwd-relative,
# #1604):
#   vcx/target/cx --allow-read --allow-write scripts/gates_register_check.cx
# BOTH GRANTS ARE LOAD-BEARING: it reads the tree and writes to stdout, and a
# denied write bound to an unused binding is dropped silently (#1608).
#
# Exit: 0 the register agrees with every suite element; 1 a refusal;
#       2 conformance/gates.cxd is missing or carries no [gate-policy].

[?lib 'cx-stdlib/io'      as=io]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/env'     as=env]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/cx'      as=cx]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/path'    as=path]
[?lib './scripts/gates_register.cx' as=reg]

# The [test-suite] element of a parsed corpus file: the file IS the element
# when it holds one top-level form, else the first [test-suite] in it.
[?def suite-of scope=private pure ($t)
  [?if [= [$name $t] "test-suite"]
    [then $t]
    [else [$first [?for [in $s $t//test-suite] [yield $s]]]]]]

[?def header scope=private impure ($suite::string $module::string $file::string)
  [?let
    [= $s [$suite-of [$cx:parse [$io:read-file $file]]]]
    [suite-header suite=$suite module=$module file=$file
                  gate=[$string [?else $s@gate ""]]
                  reason=[$string [?else $s@reason ""]]]]]

[?if [not [$io:is-file "conformance/gates.cxd"]]
  [then [?let [= $_e [$io:write-line [$env:stderr]
                       "gates_register_check: no conformance/gates.cxd under the working directory -- run from the checkout root"]]
          [$env:exit 2]]]
  [else
    [?let
      [= $doc [$cx:parse [$io:read-file "conformance/gates.cxd"]]]
      [= $policies [?for [in $p $doc//gate-policy] [yield $p]]]
      [= $module-headers
        [?for [in $dir ("stdlib", "platform", "x", "xap")]
              [in $f [$io:glob [$concat "conformance/" $dir "/*.cxd"]]]
          [yield [$header "stdlib" [$path:stem $f] $f]]]]
      [= $package-headers
        [?for [in $f [$io:glob "packages/*/*.test.cxd"]]
          [= $pkg [$path:basename [$path:dirname $f]]]
          [where [= [$path:basename $f] [$concat $pkg ".test.cxd"]]]
          [yield [$header "packages" $pkg $f]]]]
      [?if [= [$count $policies] 0]
        [then [?let [= $_e [$io:write-line [$env:stderr]
                             "gates_register_check: conformance/gates.cxd carries no [gate-policy …]"]]
                [$env:exit 2]]]
        [else
          [?let
            [= $v [$reg:check [$first $policies]
                              [suites [?splice $module-headers] [?splice $package-headers]]]]
            [= $_w [$io:write-line [$env:stdout] [$reg:report $v]]]
            [$env:exit [?if [$reg:ok $v] [then 0] [else 1]]]]]]]]]
